            <ArticleTitle>Epidemiologic studies on Theileria equi infections for grazing horses in Ili of Xinjiang province.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-113</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0304-4017(17)30314-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.vetpar.2017.07.014</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In order to found the epidemiological situation of T. equi in the horse herds in Ili Prefecture of Xinjiang Province, 723 blood samples collected from 4 counties and districts were test for T. equi through microscopic detection and Polymerase chain Reaction (PCR). In the result, we found that the 295 of 723 blood samples (40.8%) were positive for T. equi infection. The results showed that the choosed counties have a varying degrees infection. To our knowledge, this is the first time that we detected T. equi infection using the molecular techniques from Ili in Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous region.</AbstractText>
